__pycache__/
*.pyc
sources/*.pdf
docs/rulebook.pdf
experiments/results.jsonl
experiments/champion.json
# The Rust league's live champions (docs/RUST_LEAGUE.md) -- rewritten every
# few minutes by `climb`. Was assumed already-ignored (analysis/frozen/
# README.md, docs/HAZARDS.md's "never git add -A") but had no actual pattern
# here; a bare `git add experiments/` would have committed one.
experiments/rust_champion_*.json
# A local, frozen COPY of the live champions above, taken once so a
# dump_selfplay run plays a fixed set of weights even while `climb` keeps
# rewriting the live files mid-run (bots::neural::dump's top doc comment /
# the calling task's own instruction). Same reason as the pattern above:
# never meant to be committed.
experiments/policy_seed/
experiments/logs/
experiments/baselines.jsonl
experiments/league_state/
# Trainer output is never committed (docs/RUST_LEAGUE.md "Do not run git commands").
# These are the snapshots taken before a retarget -- `archive_preplan/`,
# `archive_prehorizon/`, `archive_2p_quiescent_20260729/` -- plus the frozen
# vectors the pool's `hall` tier reads.  Multi-MB, and regenerated by nothing.
experiments/archive_*/
experiments/hall_of_fame/
experiments/league_2p/
experiments/league_3p/
experiments/league_4p/
games/

# Neural value-net checkpoints and self-play data (kept on the 3090 desktop,
# not committed -- see docs/NEURAL_EVAL.md). Multi-hundred-MB artifacts.
checkpoints/
*.pt
data/
data2/

# The neural loop's working directories on the desktop training node. These are
# regenerated output -- self-play shards, per-worker logs, the master log and
# the learning curve -- and some are multi-GB. They are listed because the
# desktop is now a real clone of this repo rather than a hand-copied tree (that
# is how its engine/ silently fell two days behind), and `git status` there has
# to be readable or nobody will look at it.
loop/
loop2/
iterdata/
iterdata2/
teacherdata/
evalout/
rankdata/
probe/
smoke/
archive/

# Agent scratch: transcripts and ephemeral worktrees, never part of the project.
.claude/
rust/logs/
rust/pgo/
*.ckpt

# Built by app/build.sh from rust/ttawasm. A megabyte of binary that changes
# on every champion promotion does not belong in history.
app/tta.wasm
app/serve.log

# BGO corpus journals extracted from tar.gz for analysis (regenerated, not committed)
sources/bgo/journals/

# The BGO corpus and the third-party reference material live in the PRIVATE
# repo ptarjan/tta-ai-sources: CGE and BGA copyright, plus 1011 scraped games
# under real players' account names. Symlink it in as `sources/` to run the
# replayer or any corpus tool. It must never be committed here.
# No trailing slash: `sources` here is a SYMLINK into the private checkout,
# and git sees a symlink as a file, so a `sources/` pattern would not match it
# and it would sit in `git status` inviting a `git add`.
sources
